cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, together with the
  paper it formalizes. Scott Armstrong was supported by the European Research
  Council (ERC) under the European Union's Horizon Europe research and
  innovation programme, grant agreement No. 101200828. Vlad Vicol was partially
  supported by the Collaborative NSF grant DMS-2307681 and by a Simons
  Investigator Award.
title: "CIVAxisymmetric: a Lean 4 formalization of the regularity of asymptotically axisymmetric solutions to the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with analytic forcing"
version: "1.0"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the main results of
  Constantin, Ignatova and Vicol, "Regularity of asymptotically axisymmetric
  solutions to the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with analytic forcing"
  (arXiv:2609.20803): a suitable weak solution on the unit parabolic cylinder,
  smooth before the blow-up time, whose force is bounded in C^2 and spatially
  real analytic, whose angular mean satisfies anisotropic Type II bounds and
  which is exactly axisymmetric on a core around the axis at every time, is
  axisymmetric and regular at the putative singular point. The thirteen
  formalized results, including the interior analyticity theorem of Kahane,
  the interior estimates of Serrin and the regularity criterion of Gustafson,
  Kang and Tsai in the forms the paper uses, are proved using only the
  standard axioms, on top of the Lean formalization of the
  Caffarelli-Kohn-Nirenberg theorem, with Mathlib-only comparator challenges
  for five of them.
